## Legitimate extensions

The scalar enrichment and support bridge add a chosen A coefficient structure and a nonzero-support rule not present in B. The chain-ring classification works with free modules, Smith factors and complete basis support, not just one-hot logical pairing. The exact modal query theorems concern an oracle and an operational measurement model not studied in B. These are substantively different questions, even when their implementation is Boolean.

The new S1/S2 comparisons are evidence for B's empirical boundary. They do not change its correct same-frame identity and do not yet meet its frozen confirmatory evaluation requirements. Add a visibly exploratory mechanism/equality section or supplementary note, and retain a clear separation from any future confirmatory campaign.

## Duplication risks

Do not reprint the LM outer-product expansion as a main theorem in P01. Do not claim the truth-vector/ANF transform as a new bridge. Do not rename the cyclic group algebra as an undiscovered Boolean number system. Do not insert a familiar MQT Bell protocol as the headline novelty of P01. Do not give the same d*h theorem a full new-contribution presentation in both P01 and a laboratory paper. Expository recall is fine; parallel novelty claims are not.

## Empirical implementation boundary

The focused 105 passing tests and exhaustive signed-fusion checks in B refer to its own implementation surface. This session reran a different supplied four-arm benchmark implementation and its 12 tests. It did not locate and execute B's exact 105-test suite as a separate implementation. B's proofs were inspected; its reported test counts are inherited evidence, not added to the 102 fresh named tests.

The earlier 29-page manuscript is historical evidence. Its physical-measurement language, size claims and ordinary-modulo equivalence are not the current B semantics. B explicitly replaces or limits them.
